}

docs {
  ADR-0011's task→(model, effort) decision. The types the table knows:
  `mechanical`, `investigation`, `implementation`, `critic`.

  **The rationale comes along, and it is the part that matters.** It carries the
  provenance (`ADR-0011 §3 (a draft — calibrate with telemetry, P-7)`) and the row's
  why. Without it nobody audits or recalibrates the ruler.

  An unknown type falls to the EXPENSIVE side and SAYS that it did — in doubt there
  is no saving, because the spend shows up in the measurement and the opposite does
  not.
}
